    "answer": {
      "text": "The evidence does not contain any management discussion (MD&A) explaining the cause of the revenue change, so the 'why' cannot be supported. The reported segment data decompose the $50,115 million increase as follows: Intelligent Cloud revenue rose from $106,265M to $137,791M (+$31,526M), Productivity and Business Processes rose from $120,810M to $139,996M (+$19,186M), and More Personal Computing fell from $54,649M to $54,052M (-$597M), summing to the total change from $281,724M to $331,839M. These segment figures are reported; the attribution of the increase primarily to Intelligent Cloud is arithmetic inference from that reported data, not a stated causal explanation.",
